#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:70
#: 294994d5e74242b4a24083141b3c3b50
msgid "Starting services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:73
#: d9a229d95b184673a83e5d74378e9201
msgid ""
"The Debian way (generally) is to start daemons if they are installed. This "
"means that if you install (say) ssh-server in a template, *all* the qubes "
"that use that template will run a ssh server when they start. (They will, "
"naturally, all have the same server key.) This may not be what you want."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:75
#: 3a49275ae3634611a88da3c6672370d5
msgid ""
"So be very careful when installing software in Templates - if the daemon "
"spawns outbound connections then there is a serious security risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:77
#: 8f82b18423d24ef48a0b12ab84d14ed0
msgid "In general, a reasonable approach would be, (using ssh as example):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:79
#: 529701fe3a824143bb8a9a7a86c991fd
msgid "Install the ssh service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:81
#: 972dc9afc11141d4b73132e813dcd671
msgid "``systemctl stop ssh``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:83
#: f4b4b7af9b384182b91753521bacbe12
msgid "``systemctl disable ssh``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:85
#: 2ffa3bf7f1d742f287f19e920ee83c14
msgid "``systemctl mask ssh``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:87
#: e1d8621fcedb49d08969cf58522b0075
msgid "Close down template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:91
#: 68c89616559b425094b0a8f5f0d41cc9
msgid "Now the ssh service will **NOT** start in qubes based on this template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:93
#: d4b4214e20064516a610efa626d51b3a
msgid ""
"Where you **DO** want the service to run, put this in ``/rw/config/"
"rc.local``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:102
#: 826cf8d5d84442999dc809f8e9990d73
msgid "Don’t forget to make the file executable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:105
#: c7984c0100584d6592ba74763cc94cb4
msgid "Unattended Upgrades"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/debian/debian.rst:108
#: da56e43e1a24427aa5fba440944b7645
msgid ""
"Some users have noticed that on upgrading Debian templates, the ``unattended-"
"upgrade`` package is installed. This package is pulled in as part of a "
"Recommend chain, and can be purged. The lesson is that you should carefully "
"look at what is being installed to your system, particularly if you run "
"``dist-upgrade``."
msgstr ""

